-- title:
--   Genus invariance under algebraically closed constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $K'$, $F'$ be fields with algebra maps $K \to F$, $K' \to F'$, $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$ and $K \to F'$, the last compatible with the towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$, and suppose $K$ and $K'$ are algebraically closed. Assume $F$ is a function field of one variable over $K$ in the sense that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ and $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$, and likewise that some $x \in F'$ is transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $K'(x)$. Assume further that $F/K$ and $F'/K'$ both satisfy `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero element has an associated divisor recording its orders at all places and of degree $0$, each place having residue field finite over the base field, and the module of Kähler differentials of the function field over the base field free of rank one. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Finally, assume the $K'$-intermediate field of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$. Then the two adelic genera agree: $\dim_{K'} H^1(0) = \dim_K H^1(0)$, that is, `genusFF K' F' = genusFF K F`, where the genus is the dimension over the base field of the repartition cohomology group $H^1$ of the zero divisor.
--
--   This is the invariance of the genus of an algebraic function field of one variable under extension of an algebraically closed constant field, in arbitrary characteristic, formulated for the adelic (repartition) definition of the genus. It is used throughout the curve-theoretic part of the development, for instance in comparing orders of divisors after a constant field extension and in the Abel–Jacobi and point-counting statements over finite fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed (K F K' F' : Type*)
    [Field K] [Field F] [Field K'] [Field F'] [Algebra K F] [Algebra K' F']
    [Algebra K K'] [Algebra F F'] [Algebra K F'] [IsScalarTower K K' F'] [IsScalarTower K F F']
    [IsAlgClosed K] [IsAlgClosed K']
    (hfg : ∃ x : F, Transcendental K x ∧ FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F)
    (hfg' : ∃ x : F', Transcendental K' x ∧
      FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K' ({x} : Set F')) F')
    [IsCurveOver K F] [IsCurveOver K' F']
    (hgen : IntermediateField.adjoin K' (Set.range (algebraMap F F')) = ⊤) :
    genusFF K' F' = genusFF K F := by sorry
